# House config hub

Canonical registry: `C:\Users\Edouard\Projects\house-master-engine`

This repo (**house-lib**) is a shared Python package for the house automation stack (not a Docker service).

When you change the public API, install/deploy story, or VERSION, also update house-master-engine:

| Change | Update in house-master-engine |
|--------|-------------------------------|
| Public API / modules | `docs/inventory.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/optimization.md`; `catalog.nodes` for house-lib if purpose/deps change |
| NAS install / staging | `scripts/deploy-nas-remote.sh`, `docs/deploy-workflow.md` |
| VERSION bump | Consumers pin/rebuild; shore-up / optimization status |
| New dependency from a consumer | Consumer updates hub `catalog.nodes` (`depends_on`) |

**Stack map:** before guessing ownership across the stack, read hub `catalog` / `GET /api/registry` / `#/stack`.

**Never put secrets in house-lib.**

When bumping `VERSION`, update `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.

Before finishing, ask: "Did I update house-master-engine?"
